---
import { withBase } from "../../../site.config.mjs";
---

<section class="pi-section pi-profile" aria-labelledby="pi-profile-title">
  <div>
    <p class="pi-kicker">One profile, two front ends</p>
    <h2 id="pi-profile-title">Your terminal Pi setup comes with you</h2>
    <p>
      By default the app uses <code>~/.pi/agent</code> — the same profile as terminal Pi. Sessions,
      credentials, extensions, settings, skills and themes are shared in both directions, so you can
      start a session in the app and continue it in the terminal (or the other way around).
    </p>
    <p>
      Prefer a clean separation? Onboarding offers an app-private profile. Either way, the choice is
      an app preference: it never rewrites your Pi <code>settings.json</code>.
    </p>
    <a class="pi-text-link" href={withBase("/guide/getting-started/#choose-a-pi-profile")}>
      How profiles work →
    </a>
  </div>
  <pre class="pi-profile__diagram" aria-label="Shared profile diagram"><code>~/.pi/agent
├─ sessions/       both front ends
├─ settings.json   both read/write
├─ auth.json       shared credentials
└─ extensions/     same packages

terminal Pi  ⇄  Pi Desktop</code></pre>
</section>
